{
  "info": {
    "name": "Football Fixer",
    "description": "Uni Football Fixer \u2014 the whole flow against the docker-compose stack, in demo order.\n\nStart the stack first:\n\n    docker compose up -d\n\nThen hit **Run collection**, or click requests 01 \u2192 10 in order. Every request saves what the next one needs (tokens, team ids, match id, invite id) into collection variables, so nothing has to be copied by hand.\n\nThe two requests that matter most are **06** and **10**: both read a field that was written by a RabbitMQ consumer *after* the earlier response already returned. If those pass, the event bus works.\n\nMail goes to Mailpit, not to anyone's real inbox \u2014 open http://localhost:8025 to see it.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "gateway",
      "value": "http://localhost:3000",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "mailpit",
      "value": "http://localhost:8025",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "hostEmail",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "hostPassword",
      "value": "hostpass123",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "hostToken",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "hostRefresh",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "hostTeamId",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "challengerEmail",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "challengerPassword",
      "value": "guestpass123",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "challengerToken",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "challengerTeamId",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "matchId",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "inviteId",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "runStamp",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "kickoff",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "mailAttempt",
      "value": "0",
      "type": "string"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "00 \u2014 Gateway health",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('gateway is up (200)', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "pm.test('redis is reachable', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().redis).to.eql('ready'));",
              "// Fresh stamp per run so teams and emails are unique and the run is repeatable.",
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('runStamp', String(Date.now()));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{gateway}}/health",
          "host": [
            "{{gateway}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "health"
          ]
        },
        "description": "The only published port in the whole stack. Registered BEFORE the rate limiter on purpose \u2014 a 10-second health probe is 90 requests per 15 minutes on its own, so behind the limiter the probe would start returning 429 and mark a healthy gateway unhealthy."
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "01 \u2014 Register host team",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "prerequest",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "const stamp = pm.collectionVariables.get('runStamp') || String(Date.now());",
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('runStamp', stamp);",
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('hostEmail', `host.${stamp}@example.com`);"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('registered (201)', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
              "pm.test('tokens issued on registration', () => {",
              "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().accesstoken).to.be.a('string');",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"teamName\": \"IIIT Una FC {{runStamp}}\",\n  \"collegeName\": \"IIIT Una\",\n  \"email\": \"{{hostEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{hostPassword}}\"\n}"
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{gateway}}/v1/auth/register",
          "host": [
            "{{gateway}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "v1",
            "auth",
            "register"
          ]
        },
        "description": "The password is hashed with argon2id in a Mongoose pre-save hook, guarded by isModified('password') \u2014 without that guard, a later save of an unrelated field (the logoUrl written by the profile-photo event) would re-hash the already-hashed password and lock the team out.\n\nRegistration refuses a duplicate on EITHER email or team name, so two colleges can't claim the same team name with different addresses."
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "02 \u2014 Login host team",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('logged in (200)', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "const j = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('hostToken', j.accesstoken);",
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('hostRefresh', j.refreshtoken);",
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('hostTeamId', j.team);",
              "pm.test('access token saved', () => pm.expect(j.accesstoken).to.be.a('string'));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{hostEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{hostPassword}}\"\n}"
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{gateway}}/v1/auth/login",
          "host": [
            "{{gateway}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "v1",
            "auth",
            "login"
          ]
        },
        "description": "Returns a 15-minute access token and a 7-day refresh token. The refresh token is stored in Mongo with an expiresAt; the access token is never stored anywhere, which is exactly why it can't be revoked before it expires."
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "03 \u2014 Register challenger team",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "prerequest",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "const stamp = pm.collectionVariables.get('runStamp') || String(Date.now());",
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('challengerEmail', `challenger.${stamp}@example.com`);"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('registered (201)', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"teamName\": \"IIT Ropar FC {{runStamp}}\",\n  \"collegeName\": \"IIT Ropar\",\n  \"email\": \"{{challengerEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{challengerPassword}}\"\n}"
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{gateway}}/v1/auth/register",
          "host": [
            "{{gateway}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "v1",
            "auth",
            "register"
          ]
        },
        "description": "The other side of the Ropar story \u2014 the team that has to find you and ask for a game."
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "04 \u2014 Login challenger team",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('logged in (200)', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "const j = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('challengerToken', j.accesstoken);",
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('challengerTeamId', j.team);"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{challengerEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{challengerPassword}}\"\n}"
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{gateway}}/v1/auth/login",
          "host": [
            "{{gateway}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "v1",
            "auth",
            "login"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "05 \u2014 Create match (host posts a fixture)",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "prerequest",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "// Kick-off a week out, so the fixture reads as plausible on screen.",
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('kickoff', new Date(Date.now() + 7 * 864e5).toISOString());"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('match created (201)', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
              "const j = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('matchId', j._id);",
              "pm.test(\"status is 'open'\", () => pm.expect(j.status).to.eql('open'));",
              "pm.test('teamName is EMPTY in this response (written later, over RabbitMQ)', () => {",
              "  pm.expect(j.teamName === undefined || j.teamName === null || j.teamName === '').to.be.true;",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          },
          {
            "key": "Authorization",
            "value": "Bearer {{hostToken}}"
          }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"matchTime\": \"{{kickoff}}\",\n  \"location\": \"IIIT Una Ground A\"\n}"
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{gateway}}/v1/match/create-match",
          "host": [
            "{{gateway}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "v1",
            "match",
            "create-match"
          ]
        },
        "description": "SHOW THIS RESPONSE. teamName and collegeName come back empty.\n\nThat is not a bug \u2014 the team lives in identity-service's database, so match-service publishes `fetchTeamDetails`, identity answers on `TeamDetails`, and a consumer writes the cached copy a few milliseconds after this response has already gone out. Request 06 is where it shows up.\n\nThat gap between 05 and 06 is eventual consistency, visible on screen."
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "06 \u2014 List open matches  \u2190 CROSSES RABBITMQ",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('matches listed (200)', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "const body = pm.response.json();",
              "const list = Array.isArray(body) ? body : (body.matches || []);",
              "const mine = list.find(m => m._id === pm.collectionVariables.get('matchId'));",
              "pm.test('our match is in the list', () => pm.expect(mine).to.be.an('object'));",
              "pm.test('teamName NOW populated \u2014 written by a RabbitMQ consumer', () => {",
              "  pm.expect(mine.teamName).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty;",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Authorization",
            "value": "Bearer {{challengerToken}}"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{gateway}}/v1/match/get-matches",
          "host": [
            "{{gateway}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "v1",
            "match",
            "get-matches"
          ]
        },
        "description": "THE MONEY REQUEST. The same match that came back with no teamName in 05 now has one.\n\nNothing in the HTTP path wrote it. match-service asked identity-service over the bus and a consumer filled it in. This is the only assertion in the collection that can detect a broken event handler \u2014 a type checker can't reach across the bus, and the earlier HTTP response didn't reflect it.\n\nNote: no index on Match.status or Match.teamId, so this listing is a collection scan. Known, D-MT-08."
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "07 \u2014 Challenger sends an invite",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('invite created (201)', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
              "const j = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('inviteId', j._id);",
              "pm.test(\"invite is 'pending'\", () => pm.expect(j.status).to.eql('pending'));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          },
          {
            "key": "Authorization",
            "value": "Bearer {{challengerToken}}"
          }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{}"
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{gateway}}/v1/match/send-invite/{{matchId}}",
          "host": [
            "{{gateway}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "v1",
            "match",
            "send-invite",
            "{{matchId}}"
          ]
        },
        "description": "Writes the invite as pending, enriches both teams, publishes a `notification` event, returns 201. The email happens after the response \u2014 notification-service could be completely down right now and this would still return 201.\n\nSend it twice: the second one fails on the unique compound index {senderTeamId, matchId}. Worth showing, and worth admitting the client gets a raw Mongo E11000 as a 500 when it should be a 409."
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "07b \u2014 Invite email actually delivered  \u2190 CROSSES SMTP",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "prerequest",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "// The email is sent AFTER the 201 from request 07 \u2014 a consumer picks the event off",
              "// RabbitMQ and sends it. So give it a moment before asking Mailpit, the same way",
              "// scripts/smoke-test.mjs polls instead of sleeping a fixed amount.",
              "const until = Date.now() + 1200;",
              "while (Date.now() < until) { /* wait for the consumer */ }"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "const msgs = pm.response.json().messages || [];",
              "const host = pm.collectionVariables.get('hostEmail');",
              "const hit = msgs.find(m => (m.To || []).some(t => t.Address === host));",
              "",
              "if (hit) {",
              "  pm.collectionVariables.set('mailAttempt', 0);",
              "  pm.test('mailpit reachable (200)', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "  pm.test('an invite email reached the HOST team', () => pm.expect(hit).to.be.an('object'));",
              "  pm.test('subject is the invite', () => pm.expect(hit.Subject).to.include('Invite'));",
              "} else {",
              "  const n = Number(pm.collectionVariables.get('mailAttempt') || 0) + 1;",
              "  pm.collectionVariables.set('mailAttempt', n);",
              "  if (n < 8) {",
              "    console.log('invite email not delivered yet \u2014 retrying (' + n + '/8)');",
              "    postman.setNextRequest(\"07b \\u2014 Invite email actually delivered  \\u2190 CROSSES SMTP\");",
              "  } else {",
              "    pm.test('an invite email reached the HOST team', () => {",
              "      pm.expect.fail('no invite email for ' + host + ' after 8 attempts');",
              "    });",
              "  }",
              "}"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{mailpit}}/api/v1/messages?limit=20",
          "host": [
            "{{mailpit}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "v1",
            "messages"
          ],
          "query": [
            {
              "key": "limit",
              "value": "20"
            }
          ]
        },
        "description": "Asks the local SMTP sink whether the mail was actually DELIVERED \u2014 not whether we called our own sendMail function.\n\nThat distinction is the whole point. For months, invite emails were never sent: one `purpose` field was commented out at the publisher, the consumer's switch fell through to default, and the message acked successfully. Every dashboard was green. A mocked mailer would have passed the entire time.\n\nOpen http://localhost:8025 to read the email on screen."
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "08 \u2014 Host sees the incoming invite",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('invites listed (200)', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "const list = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.test('our invite is here', () => {",
              "  pm.expect(list.some(i => i._id === pm.collectionVariables.get('inviteId'))).to.be.true;",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Authorization",
            "value": "Bearer {{hostToken}}"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{gateway}}/v1/match/get-all-invites/",
          "host": [
            "{{gateway}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "v1",
            "match",
            "get-all-invites",
            ""
          ]
        },
        "description": "Invites where receiverTeamId is me. The team id comes from the x-team-id header the gateway injected \u2014 this service never sees a JWT."
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "09 \u2014 Host accepts the invite",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('accepted (200)', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "pm.test('response names the fixed match', () => {",
              "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().message).to.include('accepted');",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          },
          {
            "key": "Authorization",
            "value": "Bearer {{hostToken}}"
          }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"response\": \"accepted\"\n}"
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{gateway}}/v1/match/respond-to-invites/{{inviteId}}",
          "host": [
            "{{gateway}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "v1",
            "match",
            "respond-to-invites",
            "{{inviteId}}"
          ]
        },
        "description": "THREE WRITES, NO TRANSACTION. The invite becomes accepted, the match becomes matched, and every other pending invite on the match is rejected in one updateMany.\n\nA crash between any two of them tears: an accepted invite on an open match (double-bookable), or a matched match with invites still pending forever. Mongo transactions need a replica set and this is a single node, so it's an infrastructure change, not a code change. The cheap partial fix is findOneAndUpdate on {_id, status:'pending'} to make the first write atomic.\n\nRun this twice \u2014 the second returns 409.\n\nThen check Mailpit: the host and the accepted team both get 'Match Fixed!', and every rejected team gets one too."
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "10 \u2014 Match is now 'matched'  \u2190 CROSSES RABBITMQ",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('match fetched (200)', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "const m = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.test(\"status is 'matched'\", () => pm.expect(m.status).to.eql('matched'));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Authorization",
            "value": "Bearer {{hostToken}}"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{gateway}}/v1/match/{{matchId}}",
          "host": [
            "{{gateway}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "v1",
            "match",
            "{{matchId}}"
          ]
        },
        "description": "The fixture is booked. End of the happy path \u2014 the five human hops from the Ropar story, done in ten requests and two emails."
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "Auth is enforced",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "A1 \u2014 No token \u2192 401",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('rejected without a token (401)', () => pm.response.to.have.status(401));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"matchTime\": \"2026-12-01T10:00:00.000Z\",\n  \"location\": \"Ground A\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{gateway}}/v1/match/create-match",
              "host": [
                "{{gateway}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "match",
                "create-match"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Rejected at the gateway. The request never reaches match-service."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "A2 \u2014 Garbage token \u2192 403",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('invalid signature rejected (403)', () => pm.response.to.have.status(403));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer not.a.real.token"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"matchTime\": \"2026-12-01T10:00:00.000Z\",\n  \"location\": \"Ground A\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{gateway}}/v1/match/create-match",
              "host": [
                "{{gateway}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "match",
                "create-match"
              ]
            },
            "description": "401 means 'you brought nothing', 403 means 'you brought something and it's invalid'. The gateway is the single place in the entire system where a JWT signature is verified."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "A3 \u2014 Forged x-team-id is ignored",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('still 401 \u2014 the header alone buys nothing at the edge', () => pm.response.to.have.status(401));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "x-team-id",
                "value": "000000000000000000000000"
              },
              {
                "key": "x-internal-secret",
                "value": "i-made-this-up"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"matchTime\": \"2026-12-01T10:00:00.000Z\",\n  \"location\": \"Ground A\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{gateway}}/v1/match/create-match",
              "host": [
                "{{gateway}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "match",
                "create-match"
              ]
            },
            "description": "THE SECURITY DEMO. A client supplying its own x-team-id and x-internal-secret gets nowhere.\n\nTwo reasons. The gateway overwrites both headers on the outbound request, so a client's values never survive. And to skip the gateway entirely you would need to reach match-service directly \u2014 but under docker-compose it publishes no host port, so there is no address to send this to. Network topology IS the auth guarantee here (D-12).\n\nThat stops being true the moment every service gets its own public URL, which is what the Render blueprint does \u2014 and that's why the gateway-proof x-internal-secret exists at all, compared in constant time after both sides are hashed to a fixed length."
          }
        }
      ],
      "description": "Three negative tests. Run these when they ask how auth works \u2014 it's faster than describing it."
    },
    {
      "name": "Session",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "S1 \u2014 Refresh tokens (rotation)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('refreshed (200)', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('hostToken', j.accesstoken);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('hostRefresh', j.refreshtoken);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"refreshtoken\": \"{{hostRefresh}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{gateway}}/v1/auth/refresh-token",
              "host": [
                "{{gateway}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "auth",
                "refresh-token"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Issues a new pair AND deletes the one you presented. That's rotation: a stolen refresh token is usable once before the real user's next refresh invalidates it. Run this twice with the same token and the second fails."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "S2 \u2014 Logout",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('logged out (200)', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"refreshtoken\": \"{{hostRefresh}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{gateway}}/v1/auth/logout",
              "host": [
                "{{gateway}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "auth",
                "logout"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Deletes the refresh token. The access token stays valid until it expires \u2014 up to 15 more minutes. That's the unavoidable cost of stateless verification, and the short lifetime is chosen to bound it. True instant revocation would mean a denylist in Redis checked by the gateway on every request."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "S3 \u2014 Public team lookup (known hole)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{gateway}}/v1/auth/getTeamById/{{hostTeamId}}",
              "host": [
                "{{gateway}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "auth",
                "getTeamById",
                "{{hostTeamId}}"
              ]
            },
            "description": "No Authorization header, and it answers. The whole /v1/auth/* prefix is mounted without the token check \u2014 it has to be, because that's where tokens come from \u2014 and this endpoint rides along inside it, returning a team's email and college to anyone who asks.\n\nIt's load-bearing: match-service's enrichment calls exactly this endpoint back through the gateway, and has no user token to present when it does. Backlog item 1. Fixing it properly means giving service-to-service calls their own identity \u2014 the same change that would replace the shared internal secret. One fix closes both."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Media",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "M1 \u2014 Upload team logo",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{hostToken}}"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "formdata",
              "formdata": [
                {
                  "key": "file",
                  "type": "file",
                  "src": [],
                  "description": "Pick any image. The field name must be 'file'."
                }
              ]
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{gateway}}/v1/media/upload-logo",
              "host": [
                "{{gateway}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "media",
                "upload-logo"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Needs real Cloudinary credentials in .env. Select a file in the Body tab before sending.\n\nTwo things worth narrating. The gateway must NOT overwrite Content-Type here: the multipart boundary lives inside that header, so replacing it with application/json makes the body unparseable. That special case is the one thing the media proxy does differently from the others.\n\nAnd on success this publishes profilePhoto.updated; identity-service consumes it and writes the url onto Team.logoUrl. It's the simplest clean illustration of the whole bus \u2014 one service's write showing up in another service's database.\n\nKnown: no fileFilter and resource_type 'auto', so any file type is accepted as a 'logo'."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "M2 \u2014 List media (known hole)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{hostToken}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{gateway}}/v1/media/get",
              "host": [
                "{{gateway}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "media",
                "get"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Returns EVERY media document in the collection \u2014 no teamId filter, no pagination. Architecture doc issue 1."
          }
